@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+1. The French flag model and threshold readout — Wolpert's positional information, the founding frame for the whole topic.
+2. Mutual repression and bistability as the sharpener — the fly gap genes turning a fuzzy gradient into crisp stripes.
+3. Maternal determinants — bicoid and nanos anchored at opposite poles of the oocyte, and why the axis is older than the embryo.
+4. Hox genes and spatial collinearity — gene order on the chromosome matching body order, which is the strangest true fact in the topic.
+5. Clock-and-wavefront somitogenesis — the oscillator he reinvented, and how time becomes space.
+6. Raspopovic 2014 on digits as a Turing system bounded by Hox — the paper that vindicates his own answer.
