@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+- **Cleared:** named protein signalling as the fundamental driver unprompted. Independently proposed oscillation plus a bounding signal as the route from smooth input to discrete output, which is the mechanism rather than an analogy for it. Correctly identified that an external gradient could break head-tail symmetry, which is true in frogs and birds though not the general case.
+- **Did not clear:** could not name any sharpening mechanism when asked directly, and did not reach thresholds or mutual repression, which is the simpler and more general answer than the one he gave. Guessed gravity for the head-tail axis where the usual answer is maternally deposited and anchored mRNA, so the asymmetry predates fertilisation. Holds no named genes, molecules, organisms or experiments in this area at all.
